.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-vpn-status 1  "rev-stealth-vpn-status " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-vpn\-status \- Show the current public IP and the VPN container state
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth vpn status\fR [\fB\-\-provider\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Probe the current public IP via ipinfo.io and report the VPN container state (running / exit country / exit ASN) for the chosen provider. Useful as a \*(Aqbefore\-rotate\*(Aq diagnostic; pairs with `doctor` for leak checks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-provider\fR \fI<PROVIDER>\fR [default: surfshark]
Provider slug to scope the status query
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth vpn status
  $ rev\-stealth vpn status \-\-provider surfshark
  $ rev\-stealth \-\-format json vpn status

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Status probe completed.
  1  UserError        Unknown \-\-provider slug.
  2  TransientError   ipinfo / provider transient failure.
  3  PermanentError   Provider unsupported in this build.
  7  Leak             Exit\-IP probe revealed a leak (fail\-closed).

ENV:
  (none consumed directly by this subcommand.)
